    "done_when": "A fenced claude harness home carries the operator's user-scope MCP server declarations, so a fenced worker's first request lists the mcp__reckon__ and mcp__imas-dd__ tools again. The declarations live in the top-level mcpServers key of ~/.claude.json, which sits in the home directory rather than under ~/.claude, so the existing harness_home_files carry never reads it. Extend that carry so the claude backend can declare a file outside the claude config dir together with its key filter. Declare ~/.claude.json filtered to mcpServers in reckon/schema/flight-defaults.yaml, and do not add a second copy mechanism. The seeded .claude.json in the run harness home (the CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR a fenced launch sets) holds only mcpServers, is written with mode 0600 like its source, and holds no other key from the operator file (projects, oauth or user ids). Claude writes that file itself at startup, so the seed must be in place before launch, and a pre-existing harness .claude.json keeps its own keys, with mcpServers merged in. The claude binary cannot be run from a test, so tests/test_harness_home_carries_mcp_servers.py uses a synthetic operator home in tmp_path (the pytest fixture) whose .claude.json holds mcpServers plus a projects key and an oauthAccount key. It asserts the harness .claude.json after seeding has mcpServers equal to the source's, has neither projects nor oauthAccount, and has mode 0600. It also asserts a launch plan composed through the production launch path for a clive backend seeds it. The negative control drops the new declaration from the flight defaults, and the mcpServers assertion must fail. The tests write nothing outside tmp_path. tests/test_harness_home_carries_the_operator_config.py, tests/test_each_run_owns_its_harness_home.py and tests/test_fence_is_on_again.py add no failures against the base, with pytest basetemp outside any git repository. Gate and control logs are written under the run directory. The change is committed in this worktree.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "Carry the operator's user-scope MCP server declarations from ~/.claude.json into a fenced claude harness home, filtered to mcpServers, so fenced workers keep their MCP tools.",
